# Canonical Authority — Improvement Core Post-MTA / Architecture Routing 001

Date: 2026-09-24
Status: EXECUTED / STRICT-GAIN DERIVED CONTROL SUCCESSOR / RELATIVE CLOSE
Controller: Improvement Core

## Input sequence

1. current MTA on post-GDOS control architecture;
2. Tool Run Closure;
3. current Architecture Analysis on the MTA successor state;
4. Tool Run Closure;
5. Improvement Core selection and realization.

## Recovered job

Advance the Canonical Authority project by improving the relationship among the accepted
research object and its live derived manuscript/control surfaces without reopening the
substantive paper merely because control architecture improved.

## MTA result

MTA reconstructed the control system as a family of typed derived surfaces.

Key deltas:
- currentness, status typing, reader refinement, and abstract compression are distinct factors;
- authority and temporal currentness are orthogonal;
- reader projections form a many-to-many refinement graph;
- abstract compression is a preservation/loss problem;
- local update rules lack one project-specific synchronization topology.

## Architecture Analysis result

Three candidates tested:

A0 distributed controls only;
A2 one merged master control object;
A3 thin central surface/synchronization overlay plus specialized controls.

A3 passed strict-gain evaluation.

A2 was rejected because it overmerged distinct semantics and increased coupling/authority ambiguity.

## Realized successor

Created:

SURFACE_CONTROL_MAP.yaml
artifact id: CANON:SURFACE-CONTROL:001

Its job is limited to:
- surface registry;
- projection/derivation edges;
- protected-reference pointers;
- currentness/authority pointers;
- delta-class synchronization matrix;
- verification/consumer routing.

It does not own:
- fixed case;
- method;
- package result;
- contribution truth;
- source analysis;
- reader-order semantics;
- abstract semantics;
- currentness semantics.

Those remain with their specialized owners.

## Strict gain

Baseline:
specialized controls were semantically strong but synchronization topology was distributed.

Successor:
material upstream changes have a single project-specific map to affected surfaces and required
REFRESH / REVERIFY / RECONCILE / REAUTHORIZE / OPEN dispositions.

Preservation:
PASS.

Interaction gain:
Tool Run Closure now has an explicit project-specific consumer topology.

Complexity:
one thin overlay rather than duplicated semantic machinery.

Authority:
derived control only.

Result:
STRICT_GAIN.

## Regression

Preserved unchanged:
- CANON:ARCH:001 v1.2.0;
- A -> Q -> H[F] -> R -> B -> C;
- exact I_S target;
- second-order scope;
- purposive non-exhaustive corpus;
- PROFILE setup;
- TRACE / DISCRIMINATE / RECOGNIZE;
- package TRACE / COMPOSE distinction;
- prophecy positive control;
- package-level TRACE obstruction;
- bounded result;
- target-relative and attribution-sensitive authority implication;
- no universal negative.

Canonical research mutation:
NONE.

## Improvement Core frontier update

Global control-architecture design is now relatively closed under the current basis.

The highest-value project work returns to evidence-backed manuscript execution.

Immediate execution:
M05 -> M06-M09 -> M10-M21 evidence/source attachment and drafting.

Macro readiness:
W1/W2/W3 remain live in parallel.

The new surface map is used only to propagate future material deltas across those surfaces.

## OPEN

- automation/runtime of synchronization actions;
- delta taxonomy completeness;
- future new surface types;
- concurrency/multi-editor behavior;
- exact generic reuse of Representation Bridge implementation.

## Closure

MTA material consequences: persisted and consumed.
Architecture material consequences: persisted and consumed.
Improvement Core successor: realized.
Artifact/state/cockpit refresh: required by Tool Run Closure.
Canonical research version: unchanged.

Disposition:
RELATIVE_CLOSE.

# Canonical Authority — MTA on Whole-Chat Root Cause 001

Date: 2026-09-24
Status: EXECUTED / MATERIAL YIELD / RELATIVE CLOSE
Target: WHOLE_CHAT_ROOT_CAUSE_001

## Frozen job

Reconstruct the minimal object model needed to prevent internal scaffolding from being
mistaken for the user-requested final paper outline.

## Round 1 — object factorization

The current workflow has at least three distinct manuscript-adjacent objects:

B = INTERNAL_BLUEPRINT
A = AUTHOR_FACING_OUTLINE
M = PROSE_MANUSCRIPT

They are not synonyms.

B owns:
- control status;
- evidence ownership;
- readiness;
- reopen rules;
- synchronization;
- production routing.

A owns:
- paper goal/question;
- section/subsection sequence;
- substantive claim/content plan;
- source placement at author-decision resolution;
- reader movement;
- what each unit earns;
- final planned contribution.

M owns:
- sentences;
- paragraphs;
- transitions;
- quotations/citations;
- stylistic realization.

Material delta M1:
B, A, and M require separate object identities.

## Round 2 — projection semantics

A is not independently invented after B.

It is a controlled projection:

pi_A : B x ResearchState -> A

Protected observables:
- root paper goal;
- exact fixed case;
- scope;
- bounded result;
- seven-section order;
- twenty-one intellectual movements;
- source/function distinctions;
- method sequence;
- contribution hierarchy;
- bounded novelty;
- architecture reopen triggers only where author-facing relevance exists.

Allowed loss:
- tool names;
- tool-run history;
- controller state;
- artifact registry data;
- liveness formalism;
- synchronization mechanics;
- most readiness taxonomy;
- backend provenance bookkeeping.

Material delta M2:
the author outline is a lossy but preservation-constrained projection of the internal
blueprint/research system.

## Round 3 — author-level terminality

Architecture closure and author-outline completion are different predicates.

Define:

BlueprintClosed(B)
AuthorOutlineReady(A)

AuthorOutlineReady requires:
1. every section/subsection has one clear manuscript job;
2. every unit states the substantive point to make;
3. required source/evidence placement is decided at outline resolution;
4. section transitions are explicit;
5. no hidden planning decision remains that would change what the section is trying to say;
6. remaining work is sentence/paragraph realization, citation formatting, or genuinely new evidence.

Material delta M3:
"frozen architecture" does not entail "author outline ready."

## Round 4 — unresolved decisions attack

The current internal blueprint still marks local packets for:
- M06-M09 source allocation;
- M15-M16 evidence presentation;
- M21 novelty wording.

At author-outline resolution, these can be resolved now from current admitted research:
- H_P/H_M grouped first;
- H_A/H_L/H_G compressed next;
- H_X/H_R receive strongest dedicated treatment;
- M15/M16 use H_R then package-level result;
- M21 uses bounded intersection novelty language already admitted by the novelty map.

Material delta M4:
these are not architecture blockers for A and need not remain as open planning decisions.

## Round 5 — approval boundary

User approval is not research admission.

It is an authoring transition:

AUTHOR_REVIEW(A)
-> APPROVE | REVISE

APPROVE licenses prose population under A.
REVISE changes A and only propagates upstream when the requested revision violates protected
research constraints.

Material delta M5:
the author-approval gate belongs between A and M, not inside research architecture.

## Round 6 — closure attack

A clean author outline can still become stale if B/research changes materially.

Therefore A needs a lightweight sync rule:
- refresh on section/movement change;
- refresh on result/scope/contribution change;
- refresh on source change only when it alters planned content;
- no refresh for backend-only control changes.

Material delta M6:
author-outline synchronization should be content-sensitive, not all-control-sensitive.

## Reconstructed model

ResearchState
-> InternalBlueprint B
-> author projection pi_A
-> AuthorOutline A
-> user approval/revision
-> ProseManuscript M

with:
- B preserving control complexity;
- A preserving author-relevant content structure;
- M realizing A in prose.

## OPEN

O1 exact minimal author-outline contract fields.
O2 whether A should encode all 21 movements explicitly or group them under subsection headings.
O3 synchronization rule detail.

## Verdict

MTA_MATERIAL_YIELD_THEN_RELATIVE_CLOSE.

Next:
Architecture Analysis on the B -> A -> M handoff.

# Canonical Authority — New Toolset Blueprint Finalization 001

Date: 2026-09-24
Status: EXECUTED / BLUEPRINT FINALIZATION PASS / RELATIVE CLOSE
Controller: Improvement Core

## Job

Use the newest Improvement Core tools to determine whether the Canonical Authority
manuscript architecture is finished enough to freeze as the drafting blueprint.

This is not a request to prove the paper true or submission-ready.
It is a request to finish the plan so the next default operation is prose population.

## New tools and their native jobs

### RB-CPL-001 Claim/Premise Lifecycle Gate

Applied to every load-bearing blueprint claim.

ADMITTED:
- exact fixed Rashi/Ramban proposition pair;
- second-order scope;
- purposive non-exhaustive corpus policy;
- PROFILE setup;
- TRACE / DISCRIMINATE / RECOGNIZE;
- package TRACE / COMPOSE distinction;
- authenticated-prophecy positive control;
- package-level TRACE obstruction;
- bounded case result;
- target-relative and attribution-sensitive authority implication.

WORKING:
- exact manuscript wording;
- exact paragraph allocation;
- exact amount of formal notation;
- final nearest-neighbor novelty sentence;
- final journal-facing phrasing.

OPEN but non-premise:
- future corpus additions;
- final article-facing citation normalization where still pending;
- final journal selection;
- external peer review.

Result:
no PROPOSED/WORKING claim is silently used as an authoritative premise for the current
paper result.

### TOOL-LCC-001 Liveness Contract Checker

Applied to manuscript execution.

Reachable operation classes:
- movement evidence packet;
- movement drafting;
- section integration;
- cross-surface synchronization;
- novelty/source closure packet;
- hostile regression;
- meta-architecture reopen.

Local contract:
every packet returns one of:
DRAFT_READY
COMPLETE
OPEN
BLOCKED
SUSPEND
NO_EFFECT
REOPEN_ARCHITECTURE.

No packet is allowed to continue indefinitely merely because more research is imaginable.

Global contract:
a movement/section may advance when all blocking obligations for its reader job are
DRAFT_READY/COMPLETE and remaining OPEN items have typed reopen triggers.

Result:
no current blueprint movement has an untyped infinite research obligation.

### Scope Lifecycle Semantics

Applied to sections, movements, and evidence packets.

Section/movement scope identity is distinct from evidence obligation identity.

New subscopes can open only from:
- a manuscript job that cannot be satisfied at current resolution;
- a material source/novelty delta;
- a failed regression;
- an explicit external handoff.

No new named research tangent becomes a manuscript obligation merely by being interesting.

### Reachable Cut-Set Termination

Applied as execution architecture.

Cuts:
- each movement reaches a typed readiness disposition;
- each section reaches SECTION_READY;
- whole blueprint reaches BLUEPRINT_FROZEN_FOR_DRAFTING.

The theorem itself is not claimed as a runtime proof for ChatGPT.
Its architectural use is the checkpoint discipline:
do not confuse internal exploratory steps with macro progress.

### History-Cut Termination

Applied because readiness depends on provenance, rejected branches, and OPEN obligations,
not only the visible current file.

A movement cut is legal only when its history-sensitive obligations are accounted:
- claim status;
- source/evidence owner;
- unresolved OPEN;
- consumer path;
- reopen condition.

### Two-Timescale Termination

Applied to separate:

FAST:
evidence packet -> prose draft -> local regression -> section integration.

META:
change to canonical research method, movement architecture, or execution controller.

Default rule:
FAST work continues without META reopening.

META opens only on an explicit trigger:
- research result changes;
- source/corpus change changes package TRACE or section architecture;
- drafting exposes a missing load-bearing dependency;
- hostile review invalidates an admitted premise;
- strict-gain architecture change materially improves the paper.

This prevents routine drafting from restarting architecture research.

### Actual Transition Rank Applicability

Applied to execution ranking.

Do not require every exploratory step to reduce one scalar rank.

Macro progress measure:
ordered multiset of BLOCKING manuscript obligations by dependency depth.

A macro packet counts as progress when it:
- discharges a blocker;
- converts it to DRAFT_SAFE_OPEN with explicit reopen trigger;
- or proves it irrelevant to the reader job.

### Cooperative Yield / HREC synthesis

Applied to each packet.

Every active packet yields control after a finite semantic unit and returns typed state.
Continued work is represented as another packet, not as an unbounded hidden loop.

### Architecture Macro-Step Termination Bridge

Applied to the blueprint process.

Macro episode:
Select movement
-> close exact blocking dependency
-> draft/test
-> regression
-> closure disposition.

Macro checkpoint:
movement readiness or section readiness.

No requirement that every internal research action monotonically shrinks search space.

### Improvement Core history-cut instantiation / macro-termination campaign

Applied as controller synthesis.

Result:
the outline is frozen at the macro architecture level once:
- all seven section jobs are typed;
- all twenty-one movements have reader transitions and evidence owners;
- all authoritative premises are admitted;
- remaining OPENs are classified by blocking effect;
- every section has a typed completion rule;
- no current material finding changes section/movement architecture.

## Blueprint completion verdict

PASS relative to current evidence/control basis.

The manuscript blueprint is now structurally complete enough that the default next action
is population with prose.

The outline does not require further global architecture work before drafting.

## Remaining OPEN classes

### DRAFT_SAFE_OPEN

These do not block the blueprint or initial prose:
- final citation/edition normalization for some article-facing source uses;
- possible future additional corpus families;
- exact notation density;
- exact COMPOSE paragraph length;
- final journal-specific vocabulary;
- external review.

### LOCAL_BLOCKERS DURING POPULATION

These must be closed when their movement is populated:
- M06-M09 exact source allocation and quotation/paraphrase choices;
- M15-M16 exact H_R/package-result evidentiary presentation;
- M20-M21 final nearest-neighbor novelty language.

### ARCHITECTURE REOPEN TRIGGERS

Only:
- canonical result change;
- new source/corpus evidence changes package TRACE;
- accepted method premise fails;
- drafting reveals a missing dependency that changes reader order;
- strict-gain successor survives regression and materially improves publication value.

## Final control rule

BLUEPRINT_FROZEN_FOR_DRAFTING is not "nothing can ever change."

It means:
no further architecture search is licensed by default.

Change requires a typed reopen trigger.

## Disposition

NEW_TOOLSET_BLUEPRINT_FINALIZATION_001 = RELATIVE_CLOSE.

Next:
populate the frozen blueprint with prose, beginning at Section 1 or by the adaptive
movement/readiness routing policy when evidence closure is required.
